<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Komuch</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1918">1918</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Committee of Members of the Constituent Assembly</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Komuch, the Committee of Members of the Constituent Assembly, was an anti-Bolshevik government formed in Samara in June 1918 by Socialist Revolutionary deputies of the dissolved Russian Constituent Assembly, with the help of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/czechoslovak-legion">Czechoslovak Legion</a>. It raised a People's Army on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volga">Volga</a>, but after Red advances it merged into the Ufa Directory in September 1918, which Kolchak overthrew in November.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/komuch.jpg" alt="Komuch" width="320" height="233" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: QuadrangleDinglePingle · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Komuch.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
